            <div xml:id="d404">

                <pb facs="0384" n="374" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg374"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/1079</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant Chief of the Division of Far
                        Eastern Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">of a Conversation With Captain Roscoe E. Schuirmann of
                        the Office of Naval Operations</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-07">December 7, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Captain Schuirmann telephoned Mr. Atcheson at ten minutes of five this evening
                    and stated that a report had been received from the British Admiralty that from
                    three to five Japanese ships were attacking Kota Bharu in British Malaya (just
                    below Siam, 6° north, 102° east) and attempting to land troops there. [(]This
                    information was communicated by Mr. Atcheson to the Secretary’s and to Mr.
                    Hornbeck’s office).</p>
            </div>
